arm64: dts: h713: the HY300 Pro has no backlight device (A14)

On the HY300 Pro PB5 is the enable of the LED boost and of the fan rail
at once, and the vendor drives it as a plain GPIO high - never as PWM3
(its stock device tree names PB5 as panel_bl_en only, its vendor kernel
5.4.99 has no PWM consumer on that pin, and the pwm3 node is disabled;
analysis A14, 19.09.2026, umbau/reviews/A14.md). Writing a duty below
100 percent on that pin, as an experiment on 19.09. did through a DTB
with PB5 muxed to pwm3, switches light and fan off together; the board
manager then sees the stalled fan and powers the device off, and
systemd-backlight repeats the write on every boot.

The dtsi's pwm-backlight node is the HY310's (PWM2 on PB4, patch 0032),
which reaches nothing on this board, but it is a live /sys/class/backlight
device that systemd-backlight restores at boot. Disable it for this board
so nothing exists that could be written to by accident, and record the two
pin facts in the board file. The fan_power_hog of the dtsi stays as it is;
sunxi pinctrl is strict, so the hog also keeps any future node from muxing
PB5 away. Not dimmable on this board is the correct state until a
measured dimming input exists.

Tested on the HY310: no change (the node is overridden only in the HY300
Pro's board file). The HY300 Pro's owner boots the next TEST image with
it.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -4,10 +4,22 @@
